otto-agent-protocol ports the provider-runtime design of T3 Code
(https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code — the clone studied was at commit
cefb544af3c98224874419198c0359b652ca3c94). Ported parts: the provider runtime
event model and entities, the ACP session lifecycle and update mapping, the
Claude Agent SDK transport and decision mapping (ClaudeAdapterV2), the Codex
app-server lifecycle, item and approval mapping (CodexAdapterV2), the Grok
ACP launch flavour, the 50 ms streaming coalescing, the replay/snapshot
limits and the restart reconciliation. Later fixes ported from T3 Code
(main at 3ffd38ef7, behaviour only): #34597 (a cut-off reply reads
interrupted), #34183 (an interrupted Claude tool call is stopped, not
failed), #34912 (Stop on a turn that is still starting), #34564 (a model
picked with a steer switches the running turn), #34822 (a resumed Claude
waits for its MCP servers), #34762 (a passing resume refusal keeps the
conversation), #34505 (jobs that left the CLI's process group are stopped),
#34771 (Codex MCP startup failures as notices), #34782 (a failed ACP config
write is retried), #33604 (a resumed ACP message keeps its text), #34867
(an ACP choice and its `__other` field are one question) and the open
#31370 (Claude's context meter uses the window Claude enforces). Ported
from T3 Code main on 2026-11-16 (behaviour only): #28797 (an ACP refusal or
limit stop fails the turn), #34128 (the Mac stays awake while a turn runs), #32325 and #34934 (idle and
finished child threads release their agent process), #33151, #29208 and
#24334 (provider retries and compactions as one row each; retries are not
progress for the stall watchdog), #37335 (Grok steering through
`_x.ai/interject`), #33124 and #34181 (quote a passage of an answer into
the composer), #10439 (find in a thread), #15907 and #30257 (a private secret request card).
Ported from T3 Code main on 2026-11-19 (behaviour only): #39049 (an idle-released
thread keeps nothing loaded once its agent process is gone). The provider
switch inside a thread (`src/runtime/fresh.rs`, `src/runtime/handoff.rs`)
follows `apps/server/src/orchestration-v2/ProviderSwitchService.ts`
(`create_with_handoff`), `ContextHandoffService.ts` and
`packages/provider-core/src/server/handoffBudget.ts` (16,000-token default,
four bytes a token, whole items); its divider follows `V2LifecycleRow.tsx`.
Ported from T3 Code f58085a1 on 2026-11-23 (behaviour only): the delegation
rules a thread's first prompt carries (`src/runtime/delegation.rs`, after
`packages/provider-core/src/server/orchestrationInstructions.ts`), the
"Completion wakes this thread" hint an opened subagent returns and the
capabilities tool (`delegate_task` `next`, `orchestrator_capabilities`,
`packages/contracts/src/orchestratorMcp.ts`).
Threads
inside a thread (`src/runtime/children.rs` and Otto's Threads UI) follow
`apps/web/src/components/chat/V2LifecycleRow.tsx` (`SubagentTimelineLink`,
`SubagentNotificationLink`), `ThreadLineageWorkflowRow.tsx`,
`composerModelMentions.ts` (#31207, model mentions) and the delegated-task
completion wake (`apps/server/src/orchestration-v2/ProviderContinuationService.ts`,
`packages/contracts/src/orchestratorMcp.ts`). Its
